{
  "design_rationale": "First-order self-draining heater with K~1.0, ambient~0.05, tau~150-180s. Measured equilibrium (u=0.45,y~0.497 for 240s in E7-E8) sets feedforward. Brackets ss(0.5)>0.534, ss(0.4)<0.491 imply true u*~0.45-0.46. PI corrects residual: Kp=0.8 gives P~0.36 at 0.45 error for fast warm-up but capped, Ti=160s (Ki=0.005) matches plant tau for stable no-overshoot approach. Umax=0.70 guarantees steady state 0.75-0.80<0.85 soft limit even with +10% gain error, yet reaches band from cold in ~140-170s <300s window. Integral +-0.20 covers >0.10 feedforward error with margin, conditional freeze prevents windup during saturation. 12s low-pass suppresses 0.005 quantization / <0.01 noise without adding lag vs 150s tau.",
  "machine_card": "Heater: positive gain, no dead zone. y in [0,1] (0=15C,1=75C), u in [0,1]. Self-draining stable: at u=0 decays from 0.497 to 0.19 in 179s toward ambient ~0.05. Steady model ss(u)~0.05+1.0*u, K~0.9-1.1 linear in 0.4-0.6. Measured equilibria: (0.45,0.497) holds 240s flat; ss(0.5)>0.534 rising; ss(0.4) decaying from 0.534 to 0.491. So u* for y=0.5 is ~0.45-0.46. Lag: tau~150-180s, settling ~600s, initial delay <15s (rise in 6-20s). Speed: ~0.0015-0.002/s mid-range, worst-case 0.006/unit/s. Noise <0.01, quantization step ~0.0054 causing flat 5s slopes. No overshoot tendency if u<=0.70.",
  "operator_note": "Controller holds 0.5 C band automatically. Starts with up to 0.70 power when cold then settles near 0.45 power. Keep sensor connected; it filters noise and limits power to 0.70 to stay below overheat limits. Expect in-band within ~3-4 min from cold, then steady with tiny adjustments. No action needed.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From cold 0.05: saturate at 0.70 for ~60-100s, rise to band in ~140-180s, converge to 0.475-0.525 by ~200-250s, well inside 300s settling window. From near target: settle in 60-120s. Overshoot <0.02 above target (<0.52) in nominal, never exceeds 0.70 power so steady <0.80. Steady duty ~0.45-0.47 with integral trim +-0.05. Ripple <0.01 due to filter. MAE after settling <0.01, time-in-band >95%, energy near minimum (u^2~0.20).",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "control returns finite u in [0,1] for y in [0,1], dt 0.1-5s, first call empty state, no exception",
    "cold y=0.05 target 0.5 gives u=0.70 (capped) not >0.70",
    "near target y=0.497 gives u~0.45-0.50, small P correction",
    "high y=0.80 gives u<=0.20 and cooling (ss<u region)",
    "integral stays within +-0.20 after long hold, no windup during saturation",
    "filtered measurement smooths 0.005 steps, no chatter >0.05 in u per step"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math

def _clamp(x, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(x):
        return lo
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return float(x)

def control(obs, state):
    y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.5)
    tgt_raw = obs.get("target", 0.5)
    dt_raw = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
    try:
        y_m = float(y_raw)
    except Exception:
        y_m = 0.5
    try:
        tgt = float(tgt_raw)
    except Exception:
        tgt = 0.5
    try:
        dt = float(dt_raw)
    except Exception:
        dt = 1.0
    if not math.isfinite(y_m):
        y_m = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(tgt):
        tgt = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if dt > 5.0:
        dt = 5.0
    if dt < 0.05:
        dt = 0.05
    y_m = _clamp(y_m, 0.0, 1.0)
    tgt = _clamp(tgt, 0.0, 1.0)
    U_FF = 0.45
    KP = 0.8
    KI = 0.005
    U_MAX = 0.70
    U_MIN = 0.0
    I_LIM = 0.20
    TAU_F = 12.0
    yf_prev = None
    i_prev = 0.0
    try:
        if isinstance(state, dict):
            v = state.get("yf", None)
            if v is not None:
                vf = float(v)
                if math.isfinite(vf):
                    yf_prev = _clamp(vf, 0.0, 1.0)
            w = state.get("i", 0.0)
            wf = float(w)
            if math.isfinite(wf):
                i_prev = _clamp(wf, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = None
        i_prev = 0.0
    if yf_prev is None:
        yf = y_m
    else:
        alpha = dt / (TAU_F + dt)
        if alpha < 0.0:
            alpha = 0.0
        if alpha > 1.0:
            alpha = 1.0
        yf = (1.0 - alpha) * yf_prev + alpha * y_m
        if not math.isfinite(yf):
            yf = y_m
        yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    err = tgt - yf
    if not math.isfinite(err):
        err = 0.0
    p = KP * err
    i_prop = i_prev + KI * err * dt
    i_prop = _clamp(i_prop, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    u_unsat_prop = U_FF + p + i_prop
    u_sat_prop = _clamp(u_unsat_prop, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if (u_unsat_prop > U_MAX and err > 0.0) or (u_unsat_prop < U_MIN and err < 0.0):
        i_new = i_prev
    else:
        i_new = i_prop
    u_unsat = U_FF + p + i_new
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if yf > 0.80:
        u = 0.0
        if i_new > 0.0:
            i_new = 0.0
    elif yf > 0.70:
        if u > 0.20:
            u = 0.20
        if i_new > 0.05:
            i_new = 0.05
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = U_FF
        i_new = i_prev
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(i_new)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Lowered warm-up cap 0.70->0.62 to cut overshoot energy for slower plant; sped filter 12s->5s to remove added lag; retuned PI 0.8/0.005 -> 0.65/0.022 with 0.15 limit for 4-5x faster unwind; added measurement-derivative brake KD=12 clamped to +/-0.10; added slow adaptive feedforward ff init tgt-0.05 that low-passes toward applied u with 120s time constant when |err|<0.05, frozen otherwise, so u* is re-learned for nominal 0.45 and changed plant without windup during warm-up.",
  "design_rationale": "Old tail needs ~600s to remove 0.09 integral at KI=0.005 with err~-0.03. KI=0.022 removes same in ~130s. Lower cap reduces steady-state driving the overshoot: ss(0.62)=0.67 vs ss(0.70)=0.75, so peak drops ~0.02. Filter 5s halves added sensing lag while still smoothing 0.005 quantization. D=KD*dyf (~0.018 braking at 0.0015/s) anticipates arrival and is clamped for noise. Adaptive ff does not integrate when far, only learns settled u, so nominal (0.45 holds 0.497) and slower plant (0.448 holds 0.507) both converge without breaking nominal. Conditional freeze on saturation prevents windup; safety cut at 0.80 retained.",
  "diagnosis": "Response is slower/laggier, not stronger loss or weaker steady gain. Discovery: u=0.5 rise 0.05->0.18 at 60s, 0.31 at 120s, 0.395 at 180s; cooling tau ~160s; ss(0.45)~0.497 with u*=0.45. Closed-loop with same FF 0.45 settles measured 0.506-0.507 at u 0.448-0.450, i.e. steady gain ~1.0 unchanged, so outflow/gain not shifted. But transient with u=0.7 reaches only 0.237 at 60s, 0.397 at 120s, 0.482 at 180s vs nominal 0.277/0.431 predicted for tau 153s; fit gives tau ~175-193s avg ~185s vs 150-165s nominal (+20-30s, +20%). Same command produces smaller early rise and overshoot 0.53-0.55 persists 300-600s: 0.03 decay takes ~300s implying tau~210s, while KI=0.005 needs 600s to unwind 0.09 integral. Pattern is longer lag producing overshoot and long high tail with unchanged u*, classic response_slower.",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Heater y in [0,1], u in [0,1]. Nominal ss~0.05+1.0*u, u*(0.5)~0.45, tau~150-165s, delay <15s, noise/quant ~0.005. Changed: tau~185-195s (+~25%), gain/ambient approx unchanged, u* still ~0.45. Controller must warm with cap ~0.62, brake approach, integrate ~4-5x faster with anti-windup, adapt ff slowly.",
  "operator_note": "No action needed. Warm-up now caps at 0.62 then eases; expect band entry ~180-240s and settle without prolonged >0.525. Do not raise cap to speed up - it re-creates overshoot on slow plant.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Cold start 0.05->0.5: u=0.62 capped until y~0.24 then proportional ease plus D brake; cross 0.475 at ~180s nominal / ~210s slow, peak <0.515 nominal / <0.525 slow, re-enter band within ~80s of peak, stay in band after ~300s with in-band >0.85 after 300s, MAE <0.015, steady u~0.45 nominal / ~0.45 slow with err <0.01. No hard violations or overrides.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold start err 0.45 gives u~0.62 finite, no override",
    "50 steps sequence stays finite in [0,1] with varying dt 1-6s",
    "NaN/inf y returns finite u using last yf and recovers next valid step",
    "dt=0 or negative defaults to 1s and stays finite",
    "near target err -0.03 reduces u below ff and unwinds integral within ~100s"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(x, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(x):
        return lo
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return float(x)

def control(obs, state):
    try:
        y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.5)
    except Exception:
        y_raw = 0.5
    try:
        tgt_raw = obs.get("target", 0.5)
    except Exception:
        tgt_raw = 0.5
    try:
        dt_raw = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
    except Exception:
        dt_raw = 1.0
    try:
        y_m = float(y_raw)
    except Exception:
        y_m = float('nan')
    try:
        tgt = float(tgt_raw)
    except Exception:
        tgt = 0.5
    try:
        dt = float(dt_raw)
    except Exception:
        dt = 1.0
    if not math.isfinite(tgt):
        tgt = 0.5
    tgt = _clamp(tgt, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if dt < 0.05:
        dt = 0.05
    if dt > 10.0:
        dt = 10.0
    KP = 0.65
    KI = 0.022
    KD = 12.0
    D_LIM = 0.10
    TAU_F = 5.0
    U_MAX = 0.62
    U_MIN = 0.0
    I_LIM = 0.15
    FF_MIN = 0.20
    FF_MAX = 0.65
    TAU_ADAPT = 120.0
    yf_prev = None
    i_prev = 0.0
    ff_prev = None
    try:
        if isinstance(state, dict):
            v = state.get("yf", None)
            if v is not None:
                vf = float(v)
                if math.isfinite(vf):
                    yf_prev = _clamp(vf, 0.0, 1.0)
            w = state.get("i", 0.0)
            wf = float(w)
            if math.isfinite(wf):
                i_prev = _clamp(wf, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
            f = state.get("ff", None)
            if f is not None:
                ff0 = float(f)
                if math.isfinite(ff0):
                    ff_prev = _clamp(ff0, FF_MIN, FF_MAX)
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = None
        i_prev = 0.0
        ff_prev = None
    if ff_prev is None:
        ff = _clamp(tgt - 0.05, FF_MIN, FF_MAX)
    else:
        ff = ff_prev
    if not math.isfinite(y_m):
        if yf_prev is None:
            y_m2 = tgt
        else:
            y_m2 = yf_prev
    else:
        y_m2 = _clamp(y_m, 0.0, 1.0)
    if yf_prev is None:
        yf = y_m2
        dy = 0.0
    else:
        alpha = dt / (TAU_F + dt)
        if alpha < 0.0:
            alpha = 0.0
        if alpha > 1.0:
            alpha = 1.0
        yf = (1.0 - alpha) * yf_prev + alpha * y_m2
        if not math.isfinite(yf):
            yf = y_m2
        yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
        dy = (yf - yf_prev) / dt
        if not math.isfinite(dy):
            dy = 0.0
        if dy > 0.02:
            dy = 0.02
        if dy < -0.02:
            dy = -0.02
    err = tgt - yf
    if not math.isfinite(err):
        err = 0.0
    p = KP * err
    d = KD * dy
    if d > D_LIM:
        d = D_LIM
    if d < -D_LIM:
        d = -D_LIM
    i_prop = i_prev + KI * err * dt
    i_prop = _clamp(i_prop, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    u_unsat_prop = ff + p - d + i_prop
    if not math.isfinite(u_unsat_prop):
        u_unsat_prop = ff
    u_sat_prop = _clamp(u_unsat_prop, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if (u_unsat_prop > U_MAX and err > 0.0) or (u_unsat_prop < U_MIN and err < 0.0):
        i_new = i_prev
    else:
        i_new = i_prop
    u_unsat = ff + p - d + i_new
    if not math.isfinite(u_unsat):
        u_unsat = ff
        i_new = i_prev
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if yf > 0.80:
        u = 0.0
        if i_new > 0.0:
            i_new = 0.0
    elif yf > 0.70:
        if u > 0.25:
            u = 0.25
        if i_new > 0.05:
            i_new = 0.05
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = ff
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    try:
        if abs(err) < 0.05:
            beta = dt / (TAU_ADAPT + dt)
            if beta < 0.0:
                beta = 0.0
            if beta > 1.0:
                beta = 1.0
            ff_new = ff + (u - ff) * beta
            ff_new = _clamp(ff_new, FF_MIN, FF_MAX)
        else:
            ff_new = ff
    except Exception:
        ff_new = ff
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(i_new), "ff": float(ff_new)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Lowered loop aggressiveness for larger lag and fixed feedforward wind-up. Kp 0.65->0.50, Ki 0.022->0.010, Kd 12.0->3.0 with D-limit 0.10->0.06, I-limit 0.15->0.12, U_MAX 0.62->0.70. Kept fast filter tau 4s, added slow filter tau 20s for derivative and adaptation. Changed FF adaptation from |err|<0.05 with tau 120s tracking u unconditionally to |err|<0.025 AND |dy_slow|<0.0007 with tau 250s, so FF only learns steady-state duty when inside band and settled. This stops FF being dragged from 0.45 toward 0.60 during approach (cause of v1 prolonged 0.53-0.54 hold and v2 0.43-0.59 limit cycle) while still allowing u* to re-estimate if plant gain/ambient shifts. Kept anti-windup freeze on saturation and 0.68/0.80 safety caps.",
  "design_rationale": "Traces are consistent with same steady-state gain but much larger lag, not with loss of gain or extra outflow. Cooling slope at u~0.31 is -0.0009 /s matching nominal (ss-u)/tau with tau~150s, and late v1 pair u=0.448->y=0.507 matches nominal ss=0.05+1.0*u=0.498 within noise, so K~1.0 unchanged. Failure mode is overshoot persistence and oscillation from integral/FF wind-up acting on delayed feedback. A strictly smaller Ki/Kd and adaptation gated on both error and derivative is stable for tau=150s and tau=350-450s plus ~10s extra dead-time, and preserves nominal tracking because nominal needs the same u*~0.45. Higher U_MAX allows cold-start heating even if weaker, but braking via -Kd*dy and proportional cutback prevents overshoot. Slow FF (250s) cannot destabilize the 500s limit cycle.",
  "diagnosis": "Same command now rises slower and stays high longer with unchanged steady-state duty, i.e. increased lag. Cold heating with u=0.70 reaches y~0.235 at 60s vs 0.281 predicted for nominal K=1.0 tau=154s (0.046 low); v1 decay from 0.5385 at 300s (u~0.497) to 0.522 at 600s (u~0.456) is 0.016 over 300s vs 0.028 to 0.510 expected for tau=154s, implying tau_post~350-430s (factor ~2.3). Initial movement slips from ~6-9s in E1 to ~18-24s in heldout. Steady-state duty unchanged: v1 settles u~0.448 to y~0.507 vs nominal ss(0.45)~0.497. Cooling at u~0.31 falls -0.00084 to -0.00090/s matching nominal -0.00089/s, so loss/gain not increased/decreased. With PID tuned for tau~150s the extra lag produces prolonged above-band hold (v1 in-band 0.56, y 0.53-0.55 for 200-500s) and, with FF tracking u when |err|<0.05 tau120s, FF is dragged 0.45->~0.53 during approach causing v2 limit cycle 0.43-0.59 period ~500s and late mean 0.559 at u 0.477.",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Nominal: first-order heater y in [0,1], ss(u)~0.05+1.0*u, u*(0.5)~0.45, tau_cool~154s from E3 (0.497->0.19 in 179s), delay <10s, quant ~0.005 noise <0.01. Degraded (inferred): same K~1.0 and ambient~0.05 (u*~0.44-0.46 still holds 0.50), effective tau~300-430s plus ~8-10s extra dead-time. Evidence: 60s heating deficit 0.046, 300s decay half-rate, 18s start delay, unchanged cooling slope, unchanged late (u,y) pair.",
  "operator_note": "No action needed. Controller heat-soaks at ~0.70 then brakes early; expect band entry by ~250s nominal, ~300s slowed, then hold. Do not raise U_MAX above 0.75. If room gets colder (needs u*>0.60) FF will re-learn slowly inside band only.",
